<p>Authorization is the question that follows a login: this person is who they say they are, but may they do
<em>this</em>? <code>pop-acl</code> answers it with roles, resources and permissions, and then with assertions and policies for
the cases where a role name is not enough — where the answer depends on who owns the row.</p>
